					sending API with delivery-event and inbound webhooks. Vectis Mail ships a 40+ endpoint
					REST API: domain-scoped sending keys (single and batch, with attachments) and inbound
					webhooks that POST the full parsed message to your application, HMAC-SHA256 signed with
					exponential-backoff retry. If you want mailboxes <em>and</em> a programmable mail
					pipeline in one product, that's the gap Vectis closes. See the <a href="/api/">API Reference</a>.
				</p>
			</div>
			<div class="alt-faq-q">
				<h3>How do I migrate from Migadu to Vectis Mail?</h3>
				<p>
					Migadu speaks standard IMAP, so mailbox data moves cleanly with <code>imapsync</code>.
					Stand up Vectis Mail on a fresh VPS, recreate your domains and mailboxes, sync each
					mailbox over IMAP, publish new DKIM/SPF/DMARC records (Vectis generates the values),
					then cut your MX over once you've verified delivery. Plan a short cutover window during
					DNS propagation for small installs. Because the new IP starts cold, give it a warmup
					window before high outbound volume — see the <a href="/deliverability/">deliverability guide</a>.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

